A||||11||magnum||3.4 mods||||1||
Z||000000||magnum||04-02-2001||11:40 PM||||I going to put a new 3.4 in my Fiero. I have a friend who I'm pretty sure won't charge me too much for some mods. My question is what type of modifications can I be done (if any) to get more HP. It has 160 stock. How far can it be pushed. I will most likely only have to pay for parts so don't hold back. I already know about superchargers so exclude that one. Thanks allot!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||04-02-2001||11:50 PM||||Good question!  I, for one, would like to know how far I can put the 3.4's horsepower while still retaining a stock look.  That means Fiero intake and no NOS, turbo, supercharger, etc.  I want it to LOOK stock.  Headers, and a free flow air intake are ok.  I want the engine itself to look stock.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GarethWright||04-03-2001||01:25 AM||||Will Fiero Valve Covers fit on 3.4 Cylinder heads? I plan to do the 3.4 upgrade eventually.  Are there any major differences between the stock 2.8 and the 3.4 cylinder heads that makes it better to go with one over the other?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||04-03-2001||01:51 AM||||Here is basically all of the bolt-ons I am aware of for the 3.4 (and 2.8 for that matter).  Of course you can mod the block and heads for more Hp like any other engine but these are just bolt-ons.  I have 90% of these done, astericks mean I don't have it yet but will shortly.  Oh yeah for the gazillionth time, 3.4 heads and 2.8 heads are basically the same no major difference, just use the cleaner/lower mileage ones.<P><B>EXHAUST/INTAKE</B><P>Borla stainless exhaust <BR>304 stainless cat. eliminator pipe<BR>Ported Exhaust Manifolds/Headers  <BR>Bored out TB (52mm to 57mm) and manifold<BR>Cold Air intake with K&N Air Filter and water separator removed*<P><B>COOLING</B><P>New Radiator <BR>Low-temp fan switch  <BR>Stant 180 thermostat <BR>ASP power pulley*<P><B>IGNITION</B><P>MSD Blaster GM Coil<BR>MSD-6AL Ignition Control <BR>MSD Universal Wiring Harness <BR>Splitfire Dual Coil 8mm wires  <P><B>FUEL SETUP</B><P>19# Ford Motorsports Injectors<BR>Custom 3.4 manual tranny chip (S.J. Wynman)* <BR>'96 Corvette LT4 Fuel Pump  <BR>Holley Adj. Fuel Pressure Regulator <P><BR><B>Misc.</B><P>Cloyes double roller timing chain*<BR>EGR block off plates (since chip eliminates EGR)*<P><BR>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">   <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||Kelvin Vivian||04-03-2001||02:30 AM||||I've driven in a 3.4 conversion that looked exactly like a stock 2.8<P>I think John was the name of the guy who took me around for a spin in one of the conversions he did for a customer. In first gear, he was able to get the rear tires loose, something a stock 2.8 can't do, unless you drop the clutch.<P>The Fiero-guys that did the conversion were located in Westminster, CA...<P>I'm sure that it's FOCOA that I'm thinking about.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||04-03-2001||08:20 AM||||Here are some links that may help you out:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.s-series.org/htm/firestorm/stage2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.s-series.org/htm/firestorm/stage2.htm</A> <P>Good luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000006||Alex4mula||04-03-2001||10:18 AM||||Hey Black88GT;<BR>Are you using the Ford injectors? Where did you buy them? PN? Are you using the stock PROM with them? I want to do that in my 3.4 but have not found someone to confirm that they will work. Tks.<p>[This message has been edited by Alex4mula (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||04-03-2001||01:09 PM||||Alex,<P>I am using the mustang injectors, 19#, I have heard you can get these brand new from jegs or summit but I just got a set from ebay. The chip I am waiting for is made by S. Joe Wynman, its only for 3.4's with 19# injectors and manual tranny's.  Also a 180 degree thermostat is used with this chip and it eliminates the EGR system all together, which is great for me since I have a bad solenoid and cracked tube (over $200 when the chip was half that).  Email for Joe is fierojo@bellatlantic.net<P>hope this helps<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000008||Alex4mula||04-03-2001||01:25 PM||||Thanks Black88GT. Summit sells those for $150 a set of 8. I'll consider them. Similar from GM are over $400 (new). So, you are using now the stock PROM? Have you used those injectors from day one in your 3.4?<BR>I have 90% of those mods also in my stick Formula. Just need to fine tune more.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||04-03-2001||01:32 PM||||As of right now I still have the stock 2.8 injectors in there because I don't want to throw 3.4 injectors in there without the chip.  The chip should be here soon and the day it gets here I will install the Holley regulator also.  I will keep you updated ...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||04-03-2001||02:06 PM||||Cool... So your current setup is just like mine now but I already put the FPR. Please update us when you put in those injectors and PROM. Tks.||||reg||1
